# =============================================================================
# RevenuePilot — Trivy Vulnerability Ignore Rules
#
# WHY THESE ARE IGNORED (not suppressed carelessly):
#
# pip ships its OWN vendored copy of msgpack and setuptools INSIDE its bundled
# wheel file at:
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.12/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-25.0.1-py3-none-any.whl
#
# Trivy's Python scanner scans INSIDE .whl files and reports pip's internal
# vendored packages as if they were application dependencies. These are NOT
# application dependencies — they are pip's own internal implementation details.
#
# The vulnerable versions (msgpack 1.1.x, setuptools 70.3.0) exist only as
# pip/_vendor/* inside pip's own .whl. They:
#   - Are NOT importable by application code
#   - Are NOT on sys.path
#   - Cannot be patched via `pip install` (pip vendors its own copy)
#   - Are only patched by upgrading pip itself (pip 25.x ships msgpack 1.1.x)
#
# The ACTUAL application packages (installed by our Dockerfile) are:
#   - msgpack     == 1.2.1  at /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ ✅
#   - setuptools  == 84.0.0 at /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ ✅
#
# These ignores apply ONLY to the pip-internal vendored packages.
# =============================================================================

# msgpack vendored inside pip's own wheel — NOT an application dependency
# pip/_vendor/msgpack inside pip-25.0.1-py3-none-any.whl
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools vendored inside pip's own wheel — NOT an application dependency
# pip/_vendor/pkg_resources (setuptools) inside pip-25.0.1-py3-none-any.whl
